      {
        "ContentType": "Location",
        "SortOrder": 10,
        "Content": "The Old Rectory, dating back to circa 1760, enjoys a wonderfully tranquil setting on the edge of Timolin, a small south-Kildare village that offers peaceful country living while still being close to excellent amenities. County Kildare is considered to be one of Ireland’s most desirable counties to live in and is very accessible to Dublin City and Dublin Airport. It is synonymous with the bloodstock industry, famous for its world-renowned stud farms and busy racing calendar. The Old Rectory also lies close to the Wicklow border, the county known as the Garden of Ireland due to its unspoilt countryside with mountains, upland lakes, steep sided glacial valleys and great farmland.\r\n\r\nJust minutes away from The Old Rectory are the neighbouring Kildare villages of Moone and Ballitore, with the larger towns of Castledermot, Athy, Kilcullen, Naas and Newbridge within easy reach for full shopping, services and entertainment. Kildare Village shopping experience is also located within a short drive.\r\n\r\nThere are excellent sporting and leisure facilities in the nearby vicinity. For those with an interest in horse racing, The Curragh and Punchestown racecourses are a short drive away. Keen Golfers will also find themselves well catered for with Rathsallagh and Naas Golf Clubs easily accessible, as well as the K-Club, which hosted the 36th Ryder Cup in 2006, less than a 30-minute drive. The Irish National Stud and Japanese Gardens are both less than 30 minutes away.\r\n\r\nThere are a variety of primary and secondary schools in the local area including Newbridge College and Clongowes Wood College.\r\n\r\nTransport links are excellent with Timolin served by Local Link bus services, while nearby Athy, Newbridge and Sallins / Naas railway stations offer regular trains into Dublin.\r\n\r\nThe property is also just minutes from the M9, giving quick access to the M7 and M50, allowing easy commuting to major counties across Ireland."
      }
